<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The hub tray app's copy of apps/desktop/src-tauri/entitlements.plist
    (ADR-0077: per-app copies), whose comment records how both keys were
    found. Notarization requires the hardened runtime, which denies
    executable memory by default. The embedded daemon, maxprice-hub, is a
    compiled Bun binary, so JavaScriptCore JITs: without these two
    entitlements the kernel SIGKILLs it, and the console and every client
    of this Hub see no daemon at all (ADR-0148 section 6).

    BOTH keys are required: allow-jit alone runs a Bun binary started from
    a shell, but not one the app spawns. Tauri applies this file to every
    binary in Contents/MacOS, the app, maxprice-hub and maxprice-credstore;
    scripts/release_macos.sh asserts both keys on the bundled daemon.

    Only a signed build has the hardened runtime: `bun run build:hub`,
    which skips signing, and `tauri dev` produce binaries the JIT is
    unrestricted in. No double hyphen anywhere in this comment: XML forbids
    one, and codesign refuses the file over it although plutil accepts it.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
